# hypernix.old_oven

CodeOven wrapper with .complete() / .chat() / .fill() / .save_pt(). new_oven() for parametric models.

## Documentation pages

- [Ovens](../../#/docs/Ovens) · [MDXL source](pages/Ovens.mdxl)

## API reference

[Open the API reference source](pages/api-reference.mdxl)

### `CodeOven()`

A loaded HyperNix-family model + tokenizer ready for generation.

### `CodeOven.complete(prompt, max_new_tokens=256, temperature=0.2, top_k=40, top_p=0.95, stop=DEFAULT_STOPS, seed=None) -> str`

Continue ``prompt`` as code.

### `CodeOven.fill(prefix, suffix, max_new_tokens=128, temperature=0.2, top_k=40, top_p=0.95, seed=None) -> str`

Fill-in-the-middle: generate text that fits between ``prefix``

### `CodeOven.chat(messages, max_new_tokens=256, temperature=0.7, top_k=40, top_p=0.95, seed=None) -> str`

Run a chat turn. ``messages`` is a list of ``{\"role\", \"content\"}``.

### `CodeOven.train(dataset_path, out_dir=None, steps=1000, batch_size=2, context_length=512, lr=0.0003, weight_decay=0.1, grad_clip=1.0, log_every=10, save_every=500, seed=None, quiet=False, optimizer_class=None, use_abbicus=False, use_turbo_abbicus=False, use_stml=False, untrained_max_context=8192, segment_length=512, compute_framework=None) -> Path`

Continue-pretrain this oven on a raw-text file.

### `CodeOven.save_pt(out_path) -> Path`

Save a self-contained ``torch.load``-able bundle to ``out_path``.

### `preheat(repo_id='ray0rf1re/hyper-nix.1', local_dir=None, revision=None, token=None, device=None, dtype='float32', quiet=False) -> CodeOven`

Download (if necessary) + load a HyperNix snapshot into a ``CodeOven``.

### `new_oven(out_dir, arch='hypernix', vocab_size=32000, hidden_size=1024, intermediate_size=4096, num_hidden_layers=16, num_attention_heads=16, num_key_value_heads=None, max_position_embeddings=2048, tokenizer_source=None, device=None, dtype='float32', seed=None) -> CodeOven`

Create a new untrained oven in HyperNix or Qwen2 (Qwen2.5) architecture.

### `bake_code(source, prompt, **kwargs) -> str`

Convenience: accepts a preheated oven or a snapshot path/URL.

### `fill_middle(source, prefix, suffix, **kwargs) -> str`

Convenience FIM API — accepts a preheated oven or a snapshot path.

### `… 1 more`

Additional documented functions/methods in this module — see source.

